{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor","id":27741,"title":"[Idea] Lunars Let In Balor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T21:08:21-08:00","id":27741,"title":"[Idea] Lunars Let In Balor","content":"So, the Contagion is happening, every asshole is dying and everyone is scrambling for a solution. So, right here around the edge of Creation, at the border of Pure Chaos where most of the Lunars park their summer homes, one Moon Elder looks into the infinite possibility of the Wyld and has himself a vision, as Lunars are want to do in their old age.<br /> <br /> So, it basically spells out the Sidereal dilemma to him: 1. Do Nothing, aka Not An Option. 2. Try to fight the Contagion on yer own, aka Yeah Good Luck With That. 3. Let in the Fair Folk, aka When Did We Exchange Reason For Madness!? Yeah, Option 3 essentially establishes that the infinite possibilities of the Wyld Folk will cancel out with the necrotic stagnation of the Great Contagion and only dissolve a whole heaping big chunk of Creation, but it will be an ALIVE Creation, especially if you play your cards right. Option 2, well y'all have tried option two already, you've been trying it for a while. It hasn't been working. Then again, Option 2 is at least not 'Well, let's let in something JUST AS BAD'.<br /> <br /> So the Lunar aren't the Sidereal, they don't gather up in one place and then duke it out to see who's gonna do what. They are ringed all over Creation. So, instead, this vision just leaks out through the Silver Pact and ever individual Lunar gets to decide what to do. Thing is, most of 'em could go with Option 2. All it takes is a couple of 'em to go look at Option 3, 'Eh, better than nothing.' And suddenly you're up to your eyeballs in Raksha.<br /> <br /> So it gives Lunars something to do as a splat, something they did, something that utterly, literally, shaped Creation. Well, not quite as a splat, but individuals of the splat, emphasizing that the Lunars operate as roving packs of individuals bonded by circumstance and a desire to protect Creation. Or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","user":"God_of_Awesome","date":".  Small correction 12-12-2013, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:09:03-08:00","id":27765,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. It also supports the unique relationship Lunars have with the Raksha. I'd certainly use it as a possibility, but I'd keep it contained to the actions of a small group of Lunars, not a vision that every Lunar has. The Contagion is also a good backdrop for Lunars, doing their part trying to stem the sickness with their unique and powerful magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:40:21-08:00","id":27782,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea that someone figured out that sufficent could cure the Contagion and in previous edition the Lunars needed something like that to make them not entirely ineffectual.<br /> So I am not opposed to the concept.<br /> <br /> But the Crusade wasn't exactly a good thing either. Maybe as a last resort, &quot;If we don't let them in, there won't be anyone left.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:48:15-08:00","id":27784,"title":"","content":"The Crusade as a positive good that saved Creation from the Contagion is stupid, stupid, stupid.<br /> <br /> It is the terrifying invasion of rakshastan that almost swallowed humanity whole and rendered the world into its Wyld nature, foiling even the plans of the Underworld beings who had imagined finally killing the world. No Oblivion, only chaos.<br /> <br /> It's the one moment in the history of the setting that gives concrete substance to the fear inspired by the Courts of Madness that lurk beyond the world. It's the one thing that makes the raksha <i>scary</i>.<br /> <br /> Making it the ploy of anyone but a deluded maniac ensnared by the hungry fae would be a travesty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:52:02-08:00","id":27787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27765#post27765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea. It also supports the unique relationship Lunars have with the Raksha. I'd certainly use it as a possibility, but I'd keep it contained to the actions of a small group of Lunars, not a vision that every Lunar has. The Contagion is also a good backdrop for Lunars, doing their part trying to stem the sickness with their unique and powerful magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, f'course. One Lunar had the vision, like that same guy who had the one about the 'Byssies and 'Fernos, spread it around, and all it took was a couple circles of them to think it was a good idea to pull it off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27782#post27782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the idea that someone figured out that sufficent could cure the Contagion and in previous edition the Lunars needed something like that to make them not entirely ineffectual.<br /> So I am not opposed to the concept.<br /> <br /> But the Crusade wasn't exactly a good thing either. Maybe as a last resort, &quot;If we don't let them in, there won't be anyone left.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the &quot;Sidereal Dilemma&quot;: Do we guarantee (Sorta) Creation's survival but in a lessened state or do we gamble the whole world to keep it the way it is? Except, both options are big gambles, but ones bigger and ya don't need everybody on board with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:54:45-08:00","id":27789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27784#post27784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crusade as a positive good that saved Creation from the Contagion is stupid, stupid, stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think it's very apt that a disease born from oblivion is counteracted by the touch of infinite possibility.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:56:25-08:00","id":27790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27789#post27789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. I think it's very apt that a disease born from oblivion is counteracted by the touch of infinite possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>In part an inspiration taken from ES's commentary. Or Revlid's? It was on the last forum, discussing TAW History.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:56:28-08:00","id":27810,"title":"","content":"I admit, I never understood why the Fair Folk were stuck twiddling their thumbs until someone invited them into Creation. Why couldn't they just kick in the doors and invade Creation on their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T02:15:34-08:00","id":27844,"title":"","content":"Interesting side-angle from the perspective of &quot;the Contagion was 100% effective until Creation was swarmed with a set of rules that made 100% certainty impossible&quot;.<br /> <br /> It would follow that those areas of Creation which were not being actively tainted and swallowed up by Unshaped would still be operating on Omphalos Rules, where certainty is possible. So therefore, the only potential survivors would be those who were actively facing the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Which means the Blessed Isle should have been fully depopulated... unless the Omphalos was itself tainted. Which is a very interesting prospect in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:22:19-08:00","id":27935,"title":"","content":"Where was it where Revlid or ES brought up the idea that the Deathlords inviting in the Fair Folk to finish off Creation was actually self-sabotage? They described really well how it worked, essentially at least the Raksha's Chaos sabotaging the Fate-bound Contagion or something like that and possibly the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:38:46-08:00","id":27971,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;Church of Balor&quot; being a front for extremist Lunars who got the Raksha to invade en masse in hopes of purging the existing social order and remaking the world from scratch is a great idea. I also think having it sabotage the Great Contagion is a terrible idea, and I would actually move these two events further apart in time to keep people from questioning the interactions, as two existential threats that happened centuries apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:03:19-08:00","id":27979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27810#post27810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I never understood why the Fair Folk were stuck twiddling their thumbs until someone invited them into Creation. Why couldn't they just kick in the doors and invade Creation on their own?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposedly because the Solars had bound them in oaths not to unless permitted, or something.<br /> <br /> Also something about Thief of Words needing to teach them how to assume shaped form?<br /> <br /> Both of which completely invalidate the depiction of the Shogunate as having been constantly under threat of raksha invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:37:54-08:00","id":28414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27790#post27790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In part an inspiration taken from ES's commentary. Or Revlid's? It was on the last forum, discussing TAW History.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it? I'm new here I thought that just makes the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:28:56-08:00","id":28438,"title":"","content":"When I look at the first post I am reminded of some medical treatments like treating a wound with maggots. The Maggots eat away the dead flesh and leave the live. That might be what they were going for. In the end though I have a very unique look on Fair Folk from my own unique cosmology that makes them much, much, more and less. They are predigistive agents of something much bigger, they have destroyed and devoured over a thousands of thousands of creations. The Primordials would be put to sleep. Autocthon would become ill and hibernate, Gaia would fall asleep, the mother of all would join her in slumber, Theon, all the others would sleep and the world they made to find their golden answer would be devoured without them resisting. Then as a final repast the great devourer would devour their memories of the world they made. when it finishes eating and withdraws to pick the last morsels from it's teeth, they would awaken, and start the cycle over again.<br /> <br /> Only this time something strange has happened. When the devourer has come to dine and his digestive juices have washed upon the world it has met with resistance it has never faced before. The Titans are gone and nothing should be stopping it's meal but something is, and so it's unshaped chaos must take form, It's digestive system must enter the world and eat it from the inside. It must find out why the Titans are gone, and what these things are that push it back and keep it from the meal it has enjoyed so many times before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:37:30-08:00","id":28474,"title":"","content":"This idea hurts my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T21:48:20-08:00","id":28534,"title":"","content":"Mine or Hapless's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T22:07:49-08:00","id":28540,"title":"","content":"Maybe both. The idea the the wyld has something Bigger, Stronger and Meaner in it that beat the Primodials once but couldn't kill or maim them only put them to sleep, disolve the world they made, and then eat that memory. That it's been doing it time and time again, and it's hungry and dinner is late.<br /> The minds of the fair folk and everything they are, exist so that this thing can devour the world that the Primordials make, the world they keep making. Each time they stop to make a world for a new reason. Each time they go seeking their golden answer, but before they can find it, they are taken out of the picture. They have been doing this endless cycle so much they have forgotten what the question was. They only remember they are seeking an answer. And that suits the devourer well because the worlds made are seasoned better with strife and conflict now that they forgot their true objective is the answer to a question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:10:30-08:00","id":28759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor?p=27784#post27784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crusade as a positive good that saved Creation from the Contagion is stupid, stupid, stupid.<br /> <br /> It is the terrifying invasion of rakshastan that almost swallowed humanity whole and rendered the world into its Wyld nature, foiling even the plans of the Underworld beings who had imagined finally killing the world. No Oblivion, only chaos.<br /> <br /> It's the one moment in the history of the setting that gives concrete substance to the fear inspired by the Courts of Madness that lurk beyond the world. It's the one thing that makes the raksha <i>scary</i>.<br /> <br /> Making it the ploy of anyone but a deluded maniac ensnared by the hungry fae would be a travesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, anywho, I disagree with you Omnicron, because a big theme of Creation's past is doing one horrible thing to fight another horrible thing. The theme of Creation's present is &quot;Let's not do that again.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T10:13:50-08:00","id":28797,"title":"","content":"Both. But Hapless' has something that'd sound like a pretty scary idea for an Ishvara or that one unshaped that's suppose to be an Apex predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}